hadiths[107]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","""The prayer of the one whose prayer does not prevent him from indecency and wrongdoing is no prayer."
"2","""The prayer of the one which does not prevent him from indecency and evil deeds, it only increases him in distance from Allah."
"3","“Talking idly in the mosque consumes good deeds just as cattle eat grass.”"
"4","""Talking in the mosque consumes good deeds just as fire consumes wood."
"5","""Act for your worldly life as if you will live forever, and act for your Hereafter as if you will die tomorrow."
"6","""I am the center of good fortune for every pious person."
"7","""I have been sent as a teacher."
"8","""Allah Almighty revealed to the world: Serve the one who serves Me, and tire out the one who serves you."
"9","""Beware of the outwardly lush thing."" It was asked, ""What is meant by this?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) replied: ""A beautiful woman who has been brought up in a bad environment."
"10","“If two groups of my Ummah are set right, then (all) the people will be set right: one, the rulers; and the other, the scholars (jurists).”"
"12","“Seek means through my rank and status, for my status is very great with Allah.”"
"13","""Whoever leaves his house for prayer and says: O Allah! I ask You by the right of those who ask of You, and by the right of my walking, and indeed I have not come out in pride or arrogance, then Allah turns towards him with His Face, and a thousand (1000) angels seek forgiveness for him."
"14","""Goodness and virtue are in me and will remain in my Ummah until the Day of Judgment."
"15","""Whoever sleeps after Asr and his intellect is snatched away (i.e., his mind is taken), then he should blame no one but himself."
"16","""Whoever lost his ablution and did not perform ablution has certainly wronged Me; whoever performed ablution and did not pray has certainly wronged Me; whoever prayed and did not supplicate to Me has certainly wronged Me; and whoever supplicated to Me but I did not accept his supplication, then certainly I have wronged him, and I am not an unjust Lord."
"17","""Whoever performed Hajj of the House of Allah and did not visit me, then surely he has wronged me."
"18","""Whoever performed Hajj and visited my grave after my death, it is as if he visited me during my lifetime."
"19","""The disagreement of my Ummah is a mercy."
"20","""My companions are like stars; whichever of them you follow, you will be guided."
"21","""Indeed, my companions are like stars; so whichever of their sayings you hold on to, you will be rightly guided."
"22","""Whoever has recognized his own self has certainly recognized his Lord."
"23","""My Lord taught me manners and perfected my refinement."
"24","""All people are dead except those who have knowledge, and all those who have knowledge are destroyed and doomed except those who act, and all those who act are drowned and annihilated except those who are sincere, and even those who are sincere are in great danger."
"25","""The leftover food of a believer is a cure."
"26","""When you see black flags coming from the direction of Khurasan, then go to them, even if you have to crawl over ice, because among them is Allah's Caliph, 'Mahdi'."
"27","""The one who repents is the beloved (i.e., friend) of Allah."
"28","""Beware! Indeed, I do not forget, but I am made to forget so that I may establish the rulings of the Shariah."
"29","""People are asleep; when they die, they will wake up."
"30","""Whoever narrates a hadith and at that moment is overcome by thirst, then that (hadith) is true."
"31","""Marry and do not divorce, for divorce causes the Throne to tremble."
"32","“A prayer will be repeated due to blood equal to a dirham (i.e., if someone’s clothes are stained with this much blood and he performs the prayer, it is obligatory for him to repeat the prayer; and if the blood is less than this amount, then repetition is not obligatory).”"
"33","""The generous person is close to Allah's mercy, close to Paradise, close to people, and far from the fire of Hell, while the miser is far from Allah, far from Paradise, far from people, and close to the fire of Hell. And an ignorant generous person is more beloved to Allah Almighty than a miserly worshipper."
"34","""I am an Arab, the Qur'an is in Arabic, and the language of the people of Paradise is also Arabic."
"35","""Indeed, everything has a heart, and the heart of the Qur'an is Surah 'Ya-Sin.' Whoever recites it (once), it is as if he has recited the Qur'an ten times."
"36","""Concern for the Day of Judgment is better than sixty (60) years of worship."
"37","""The prayer of the neighbor of the mosque is only in the mosque (not at home)."
"38","""The Black Stone is Allah's right hand on earth; with it, He shakes hands with His servants."
"39","""Fast and you will become healthy."
"40","“Gabriel (peace be upon him) advised me to treat the neighbor well up to forty houses: forty on this side, forty on that side, forty on this side, and forty on that side (that is, ten houses in each direction around your house are included as neighbors).”"
"41","""(O Prophet!) If it were not for you, I would not have created the world."
"42","""Whoever recites Surah Al-Waqi'ah every night will never experience poverty."
"43","""Whoever begins the morning and his concern and sorrow is for anything other than the pleasure of Allah, then he has no connection with Allah; and whoever is not grieved and concerned for the Muslims is not one of them."
"44","""As you are (yourselves), so will rulers and governors be appointed over you."
"45","""Indeed, Allah Almighty descends to the nearest heaven on the night of the fifteenth (15th) of Sha'ban and forgives more people than the number of hairs on the sheep of Banu Kalb."
"46","It is narrated from Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that she reports from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Do you know what night this is (i.e., the night of the fifteenth (15th) of Sha'ban)?"" Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) submitted: ""O Messenger of Allah! What happens in it?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On this night, it is written about the children of Adam who will be born in this year; on this night, it is written about every human being from the children of Adam who will die in this year; on this night, their deeds are raised (to Allah), and on this night, their sustenance is sent down."
"47","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) that ""Indeed, on the night of the 15th of Sha'ban, Allah looks with mercy towards the people of the earth and forgives all His creation except for a polytheist or one who harbors enmity (without reason)."
"48","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) in a marfu’ report that: “When the night of the fifteenth of Sha’ban comes, stand in prayer during its night and fast during its day. Indeed, Allah Almighty descends to the lowest heaven after sunset on that night and proclaims: Beware! Who is there who seeks forgiveness from Me, so that I may forgive him? Who is there who seeks provision from Me, so that I may provide for him? Who is there who is afflicted or in distress, so that I may grant him relief? Beware! Is there so-and-so, is there so-and-so, until the dawn breaks.”"
"49","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) that: ""There are five nights in which supplication is not rejected: (1) The first night of the month of Rajab, (2) The night of the fifteenth of Sha'ban, (3) The night of Jumu'ah (Friday), (4) The night of Eid al-Fitr, (5) The night of Eid al-Adha."
"50","“If a child is born to someone and he calls the adhan in the right ear and the iqamah in the left ear, then ‘umm al-sibyan’ (the name of a disease) will not harm him.”"
"51","""Whoever firmly holds onto my Sunnah during the corruption of my Ummah will have the reward of 100 martyrs."
"52","“At the time of corruption in my Ummah, the one who adheres to my Sunnah will have the reward of a martyr.”"
"53","""I am the son of two sacrificial ones (that is, Isma'il عليه السلام and your Prophet's father, 'Abdullah)."
"54","""Looking at the Qur'an is worship, looking at one's parents is worship, and looking at Hazrat Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) is also worship."
"55","""Whoever offers forty prayers in my mosque (i.e., Masjid Nabawi) without missing a single prayer among them, then for him freedom from the Fire and salvation from punishment will be written, and he will be free from hypocrisy."
"56","""Close relatives are more deserving of kindness."
"57","""The last person to enter Paradise will be an individual from the tribe of Juhaina, who will be called by the name Juhaina. The people of Paradise will ask him if there is anyone left who is still being punished. He will say: No. Then they will say that Juhaina has certain knowledge."
"58","""The best name is that with which worship is performed and praise is offered."
"59","""Acquire knowledge even if you have to go to China."
"60","""Consult them, that is, women (but after consulting), oppose their advice."
"61","""On the Day of Resurrection, people will be called with their mothers for the sake of their covering (of faults), because if they are called with their fathers, it is possible that the one who was considered their father in the world may not actually be their real father, but someone else, and then in the plain of resurrection, it would be publicly revealed that he is illegitimately born."
"62","""The ruler is Allah's shade on His earth; whoever wishes him well is rightly guided, and whoever deceives him goes astray."
"63","""Whoever fears Allah, Allah will make everything fear him; and whoever does not fear Allah, then Allah will make him fear everything."
"64","Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, said: ""Whoever is not pleased with My decree and does not show patience over My trial, then let him seek a Lord other than Me."
"65","""There is no backbiting of a sinful and immoral person (i.e., there is no sin in backbiting a sinner)."
"66","“When any one of you passes away and you bury him, let one of you stand near his head and say: O son of such-and-such woman, so-and-so! Surely he will hear. Then say: O son of such-and-such woman, so-and-so! Indeed, he will sit up straight. Then say: O son of such-and-such woman, so-and-so! Surely, he will say: Guide me, guide me, may Allah have mercy on you. Then say: Remember that which you departed from this worldly home upon, (that is) the testimony that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, He is alone, He has no partner, and indeed Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is His servant and Messenger, the Hour is coming in which there is no doubt, and surely Allah will resurrect those in the graves.”"
"67","""Whoever performed Istikhara was never disappointed or unsuccessful, whoever consulted (others) was never regretful or remorseful, and whoever adopted moderation was never impoverished."
"68","""When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would cut his hair or nails or undergo cupping, he would send those hairs to the cemetery of Baqi' al-Gharqad, and then they would be buried there."
"69","""A believer is intelligent, wise, and alert."
"70","“O people! Indeed, a great month has cast its shadow over you, a month in which there is a night that is better than a thousand months (of worship). Allah Almighty has made its fasting obligatory and its night prayer (i.e., Tarawih) voluntary. Whoever does any good deed in this month will be like the one who performed a compulsory act in any other month, and whoever performs a compulsory act in it will be like the one who performed seventy compulsory acts in any other month. It is the month of patience, and the reward for patience is Paradise. It is the month of sympathy, and it is a month in which the sustenance of the believer is increased. Whoever provides iftar to a fasting person in it, his sins will be forgiven, his neck will be freed from Hellfire, and he will receive a reward equal to that of the fasting person (whom he fed) without any decrease in the fasting person’s reward. We said: O Messenger of Allah! Not all of us have the means to provide iftar to a fasting person. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Allah Almighty will grant this reward to the one who gives a fasting person a sip of milk, a date, or a sip of water to break his fast, and whoever gives a fasting person a full meal so that he is satisfied, Allah Almighty will give him to drink from my cistern, after which he will never feel thirst until he enters Paradise. It is a month whose beginning is mercy, whose middle is forgiveness, and whose end is freedom from Hellfire. And whoever eases the burden on his subordinate (slave or servant) in this month, Allah Almighty will forgive him and free him from the fire of Hell.”"
"71","“O Jibreel (Gabriel), describe for me the Fire and Hell.” Jibreel (peace be upon him) replied: “Indeed, Allah the Exalted commanded regarding Hell, so it was kindled for a thousand years until it became white. Then He commanded regarding it again, so it was kindled for another thousand years until it became red. Then (for the third time) He commanded regarding it, so it was kindled for another thousand years until it became black, and now its color is extremely black and dark.”"
"72","""Do not engage in excessive speech except with the remembrance of Allah, for excessive speech without the remembrance of Allah hardens the heart, and indeed, the person farthest from Allah is the one with a hard heart."
"73","""When any one of you reaches a row and it is already complete, then he should pull a man towards himself from the row and make him stand by his side."
"74","“In this Ummah, thirty Abdaal will be born, like Ibrahim Khalil-ur-Rahman (peace be upon him). Whenever one man among them passes away, Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, will send another man in his place.”"
"75","""Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) did not surpass you because of the abundance of his fasts and prayers, but rather because of that thing which he carried in his heart (i.e., faith and piety)."
"76","""In the House of Allah, the greeting of the mosque (Tahiyyat al-Masjid) is (performed by) Tawaf itself (i.e., for the one entering Masjid al-Haram to perform Tawaf, it is not necessary for him to offer Tahiyyat al-Masjid before sitting)."
"77","“Indeed, when a servant stands in prayer, he is between the two eyes of the Most Merciful, and if he looks here and there, the Lord says to him, O son of Adam! To whom are you looking? Are you looking towards someone who is better for you than Me? O son of Adam! Pay attention in your prayer, I am better for you than that towards which you are looking.”"
"78","A thought arose in the heart of Musa (peace be upon him): Does Allah Almighty also sleep? So Allah Almighty sent an angel to him, who made him sleep continuously for three days. Then he handed him two glass vessels, one in each hand... Then he (Musa) fell asleep, his hands moved, and both glass vessels (fell and) broke. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Allah Almighty gave him this example that if Allah Almighty were to sleep, the heavens and the earth would not remain (but would fall)."
"79","“(Looking at a non-mahram) is one of the arrows of Iblis; whoever, out of fear of Allah Almighty, refrains from it, Allah Almighty will grant him such faith, the sweetness of which he will feel in his heart.”"
"80","“Ablution will be performed again due to a flowing nosebleed.”"
"81","""Faith is not the name of mere wishing and adorning oneself, rather faith is that which weighs upon the heart and whose truth is affirmed by (the believer's) character and actions."
"82","“A beast will emerge carrying the staff (stick) of Musa (Moses), peace be upon him, and the ring of Sulaiman (Solomon), peace be upon him, and it will say: This is a believer! This is a disbeliever!”"
"83","""The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) went towards the cave and entered it. Then a spider came and spun a web at the entrance of the cave. The disbelievers of Quraysh came searching for the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and when they saw the spider’s web at the entrance of the cave, they said that no one has entered it."
"84","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) noticed an odor and said: The person with this odor should stand up and perform ablution. The man felt shy to stand up (so he did not stand), so the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said (again): The person with this odor should stand up and perform ablution because Allah does not feel shy of the truth. Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Messenger of Allah! Should we all perform ablution? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: (Yes) all of you go and perform ablution."
"85","“When my Ummah adopts fifteen practices, trials will descend upon them. (These are): (1) When spoils of war are treated as personal property (i.e., some are given from the spoils and others are deprived), (2) trusts are regarded as spoils of war (i.e., people seize entrusted property as if it were war booty), (3) zakat is considered a penalty (i.e., people find it burdensome to pay, regarding it not as purification of wealth or a divine command, but as a tax or fine), (4) every man obeys his wife (in all lawful and unlawful matters), (5) but disobeys his mother, (6) treats his friend well (and brings him close), (7) but mistreats his father (and distances him), (8) voices are raised in the mosques (with disputes, business dealings, and idle talk), (9) the leader and guardian of the people (i.e., their chief) is the most vile and base among them, (10) a man is honored out of fear of his evil (lest his harm reaches them), (11) intoxicants are consumed, (12) (unnecessarily) silk is worn, (13) singing and dancing women are taken up, and (14) musical instruments are acquired, (15) the last of this Ummah (i.e., those who come later) curse the first (i.e., the righteous predecessors)—(it is also explained that instead of performing righteous deeds, they will not follow the righteous predecessors, which is tantamount to cursing them). When the people of the Ummah begin to do these things, then they should await a red wind, and being swallowed by the earth and transformation (i.e., being sunk into the earth and having their forms changed), for they will surely be afflicted with such punishments.”"
"86","""Love of the world is the root of every sin."
"87","“Seeking lawful (halal) sustenance is also jihad, and indeed Allah Almighty loves the professional (skilled and artisan) believer.”"
"88","""Everything has a bride, and the bride of the Qur'an is Surah Rahman."
"89","""The leader of a people is their servant."
"90","""Adhere to two healing things: one is honey and the other is the Qur'an."
"91","""The poetry of Umayyah bin Abi Salt has embraced faith, (but) his heart has disbelieved."
"92","""Goodness does not decay, sin is not forgotten, and the One who takes account does not sleep. So now become whatever you wish (because surely) you will be rewarded according to the way of life you adopt."
"93","""Facing the Angel of Death is more severe than a thousand (1000) strikes of the sword."
"94","“Hasten to perform righteous deeds before seven things: are you waiting for poverty which will make you forget everything, or wealth which will make you transgress, or a disease which will corrupt you, or old age which will render you feeble-minded, or sudden death which will destroy you, or the Dajjal who is the worst awaited absent one, or are you waiting for the Hour (Day of Judgment), for the Hour is most grievous and bitter.”"
"95","""The one among you who is the most daring in giving fatwas is also the most daring among you in entering the fire of Hell. (This means that one should be cautious in giving fatwas, avoid haste, lest an incorrect fatwa is issued without proper investigation, which may become a cause for entering Hell.)"
"96","""Beware of the insight (keen perception and wisdom) of the believer, for he sees with the light of Allah."
"97","""The world is the home of the one who has no home, and the wealth of the one who has no wealth, and only the one who has no intellect gathers (its goods and riches) for it."
"98","""Do not make water the last thing you consume with your food."
"99","""Hearts also become rusty like iron, and their remedy is seeking forgiveness (istighfar)."
"100","“We have returned from the lesser jihad to the greater jihad.”"
"101","""Whoever breaks a fast on any day of Ramadan without an allowance or permission granted by Allah Almighty, then even if he fasts for his entire life, it will not make up for that day."
"102","“Indeed, Abdur Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) will enter Paradise crawling on his back.”"
"103","“The most disliked of permissible things to Allah is divorce.”"
"104","“When the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) arrived in Madinah, the women, children, and slaves began reciting these verses: The full moon has risen upon us; gratitude is incumbent upon us; O you who have been sent from the direction of the southern hills! You have brought such a command that obedience to it is obligatory.”"
"105","""Beware of envy, for envy consumes good deeds just as fire consumes wood."
"106","“Indeed, Allah the Exalted says: I am Allah, there is no deity worthy of worship except Me. (I alone) am the Owner of kings, the King of kings. The hearts of kings are in My hand, and surely when My servants obey Me, I turn the hearts of their kings towards them with compassion, mercy, and gentleness (i.e., I make the rulers’ hearts gentle towards their subjects). And when My servants disobey Me, I turn the hearts of their kings towards them with anger and vengeance, then they make them (i.e., My disobedient ones) taste a severe punishment. Therefore, do not occupy yourselves with cursing your kings, but rather occupy yourselves with My remembrance and humility; I will restrain your kings from (oppressing and wronging) you.”"
"107","""Reciting the adhan and iqamah in the ear of a newborn child."
"108","""Wisdom is the lost property of every wise person; when he finds it, he is the most deserving of it."
